        "answer": {
          "short": "The equal angles are not included between the two pairs of equal sides, so SAS cannot be used.",
          "worked": "The known equal sides are $CA=CB$ and $CP=CP$. The angles included between these sides are $\\angle ACP$ and $\\angle BCP$, whose equality has not been established. The supplied equality $\\angle CAP=\\angle CBP$ concerns non-included angles, so SAS does not establish congruence. Therefore the conclusion $AP=BP$ is unsupported.",
